<h2 id="authentication">Authentication</h2>
<p>All API endpoints require authentication via a <strong>Bearer token</strong> (JWT) issued by PiratenSSO (Keycloak), unless marked as public.</p>

<h3>Obtaining a token</h3>
<p><strong>Apps acting on behalf of a member</strong> (e.g. the iOS app) sign the user in with the OAuth 2.0 Authorization Code flow with PKCE against the PiratenSSO realm <code>Piratenlogin</code> and send the user's access token. The server identifies the user by the token's <code>sub</code> claim and creates the user record on first request.</p>
<p><strong>Server-to-server clients</strong> can use the client credentials flow. The resulting token belongs to the client's service account, not to a member:</p>
<pre><code>POST https://sso.piratenpartei.de/realms/Piratenlogin/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials
&client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID
&client_secret=YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET</code></pre>

<p>The response contains an <code>access_token</code>:</p>
<pre><code>{
  "access_token": "eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIs...",
  "expires_in": 300,
  "token_type": "Bearer"
}</code></pre>

<h3>Using the token</h3>
<p>Include the token in the <code>Authorization</code> header of every request:</p>
<pre><code>Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIs...</code></pre>

<h3>Authentication errors</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Status</th><th>Body</th><th>Cause</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>401</code></td><td><code>{"error": "Authorization header required"}</code></td><td>No <code>Authorization</code> header sent</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>401</code></td><td><code>{"error": "Invalid token: ..."}</code></td><td>Token is expired, malformed, or signed by an untrusted issuer</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Example: authenticated request</h3>
<pre><code>curl -H "Authorization: Bearer eyJhbG..." \
     -H "Accept: application/json" \
     https://meine-piraten.de/tasks.json</code></pre>

<hr>

<h2 id="tasks">Tasks</h2>
<p>A task represents an actionable item assigned to an organizational entity and category.</p>

<h3>Endpoints</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Method</th><th>Path</th><th>Description</th><th>Permission</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/tasks.json</code></td><td>List all tasks</td><td>Any authenticated user</td></tr>
    <tr><td>GET</td><td><code>/tasks/:id.json</code></td><td>Get a single task</td><td>Any authenticated user</td></tr>
    <tr><td>POST</td><td><code>/tasks.json</code></td><td>Create a task</td><td>Admin</td></tr>
    <tr><td>PATCH/PUT</td><td><code>/tasks/:id.json</code></td><td>Update a task</td><td>Any authenticated user <em>(see field restrictions below)</em></td></tr>
    <tr><td>DELETE</td><td><code>/tasks/:id.json</code></td><td>Delete a task</td><td>Admin</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Request parameters (create / update)</h3>
<p>Wrap parameters in a <code>task</code> key:</p>
<pre><code>{
  "task": {
    "title":               "string (required for create, max 200 characters)",
    "description":         "string (optional, max 2000 characters)",
    "completed":           "boolean",
    "creator_name":        "string",
    "time_needed_in_hours": "integer (optional)",
    "activity_points":     "integer (optional)",
    "due_date":            "date (YYYY-MM-DD, optional)",
    "urgent":              "boolean (optional)",
    "category_id":         "integer (required for create, foreign key)",
    "entity_id":           "integer (required for create, foreign key)",
    "status":              "string (optional, see status transitions below)",
    "assignee":            "string (optional, PiratenSSO username)"
  }
}</code></pre>

<h4>Field update restrictions for non-admin users</h4>
<p>Non-admin users may only update <code>status</code> and <code>assignee</code>. Any other fields they send are <strong>silently ignored</strong>: the request still returns <code>200 OK</code> with the unchanged values. Check the response body instead of assuming the change was applied.</p>

<h3>Status transitions</h3>
<p>Task status follows a strict state machine.</p>
<ul>
  <li>A transition the state machine does not allow (e.g. <code>open → done</code>) returns <strong>422 Unprocessable Entity</strong>.</li>
  <li>A non-admin attempting an admin-only transition (e.g. <code>completed → done</code>) returns <strong>403 Forbidden</strong> with <code>{"error": "Forbidden"}</code>.</li>
</ul>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>From</th><th>Allowed transitions</th><th>Who can transition</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>open</code></td><td><code>claimed</code></td><td>Any authenticated user</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>claimed</code></td><td><code>completed</code>, <code>open</code></td><td>Any authenticated user</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>completed</code></td><td><code>done</code>, <code>claimed</code></td><td>Admin only</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>done</code></td><td><em>(none &mdash; terminal state)</em></td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Response example (single task)</h3>
<pre><code>{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "Wahlkampfmaterial bestellen",
  "description": "Flyer und Plakate für den Wahlkampf bestellen",
  "completed": false,
  "creator_name": "pirat42",
  "time_needed_in_hours": 2,
  "due_date": "2025-06-01",
  "urgent": true,
  "activity_points": 10,
  "category_id": 1,
  "entity_id": 1,
  "status": "open",
  "assignee": null,
  "created_at": "2025-05-04T12:00:00.000Z",
  "updated_at": "2025-05-04T12:00:00.000Z",
  "url": "https://meine-piraten.de/tasks/1.json"
}</code></pre>

